+# Getting Started
+
+[← Back to Index](INDEX.md) | [← Architecture Overview](01-overview.md)
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+### Runtime Requirements
+
+| Component | Version | Purpose |
+|-----------|---------|---------|
+| Java | 22+ | Application runtime (preview features required) |
+| PostgreSQL | 14+ | Primary database |
+| Redis | 7+ | Caching, session store, DNS L2 cache |
+| Linux x86_64 | Kernel 5.15+ | Production deployment (XDP requires 5.15+) |
+
+### Build Requirements
+
+| Component | Version | Purpose |
+|-----------|---------|---------|
+| Gradle | 8.x (wrapper included) | Java build |
+| GCC / Clang | 12+ | Native C libraries |
+| CMake | 3.20+ | asciiart_linux build |
+| libbpf-dev | 1.0+ | XDP firewall build |
+| FFmpeg dev libs | 6+ | Video decode in asciiart |
+| WSL2 (Windows) | Ubuntu 22.04+ | Building Linux native libs on Windows |
+
+## Building the Project
+
+### 1. Java Application (Gradle)
+
+```bash
+# Build the fat JAR (includes native libs if pre-built)
+./gradlew bootJar
+
+# Build with XDP (requires WSL on Windows)
+./gradlew buildWithXdp
+```
+
+The build automatically:
+- Copies native libraries from `skibidi_generator_build/`, `skibidi_inferx_build/`, `asciiart_build/`, `xdp_build/` into the JAR
+- Packages SkibidiInferX model files (`skibidi_ai.safetensors`, `tokenizer.json`)
+- Organizes platform-specific libraries into `native/{platform}/` directories
+
+### 2. Native Libraries
+
+#### Skibidi Generator (AVX2/AVX-512 expression generator)
+
+```bash
+# Linux
+cd skibidi_generator
+./build_native.sh
+
+# Windows (PowerShell)
+cd skibidi_generator
+./build.ps1
+```
+
+Output: `skibidi_generator_build/libskibidi_avx.so` (or `.dll`)
+
+#### SkibidiInferX Native (Transformer inference kernels)
+
+```bash
+# Linux
+cd skibidi_inferx_native/native_linux
+./build.sh
+
+# Windows
+cd skibidi_inferx_native/native_win
+./build.cmd
+```
+
+Output: `skibidi_inferx_build/libskibidi_inferx_native.so` (or `.dll`)
+
+#### ASCII Art Library (Video→ASCII/Minecraft maps)
+
+```bash
+cd asciiart_linux
+mkdir build && cd build
+cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+make -j$(nproc)
+```
+
+Output: `asciiart_build/libasciiart.so`
+
+Dependencies: FFmpeg (libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil, libswscale), optionally Cairo + FreeType for mail rendering.
+
+#### XDP Firewall (eBPF kernel firewall)
+
+```bash
+cd lmyzmail-xdp
+./build.sh all
+# Or use make directly:
+make all
+```
+
+Output: `.build/liblmyzmail_xdp.so` + `.build/xdp_firewall.bpf.o`
+
+Requires: `libbpf-dev`, `clang`, `bpftool`, Linux kernel headers with BTF support.
+
+### 3. AI Model (SkibidiInferX LM)
+
+The model files should be placed at:
+```
+skibidi-lm-model/SkibidiLM_260409_22M_1M2_Samples_128/
+├── skibidi_ai.safetensors    # Model weights (~22M parameters)
+└── tokenizer.json            # BPE tokenizer vocabulary
+```
+
+These are automatically copied to `build/resources/main/skibidi-inferx-model/` during build.
+
+## Deployment
+
+### Automated Deployment (Ubuntu 24.04)
+
+```bash
+sudo ./deploy.sh
+```
+
+The script handles:
+1. System updates and dependency installation (JDK 21, PostgreSQL, Nginx, Certbot)
+2. DNS verification for your domain
+3. JAR download and placement at `/opt/botmail/botmail.jar`
+4. PostgreSQL database and user creation
+5. System user (`botmail`) and directory structure
+6. DKIM key generation (RSA 2048-bit)
+7. Application properties generation
+8. SSL certificate (Let's Encrypt with self-signed fallback)
+9. Nginx reverse proxy configuration
+10. Systemd service setup and startup
+
+### Manual Deployment
+
+```bash
+# 1. Create directories
+mkdir -p /opt/botmail/logs
+mkdir -p /var/lib/botmail/data/mail
+mkdir -p /var/lib/botmail/dkim
+mkdir -p /var/lib/botmail/ssl
+
+# 2. Place files
+cp build/libs/botmail-2.8.0.jar /opt/botmail/botmail.jar
+cp application.properties /opt/botmail/
+
+# 3. Generate DKIM keys
+openssl genrsa -out /var/lib/botmail/dkim/private.pem 2048
+openssl rsa -in /var/lib/botmail/dkim/private.pem -pubout -out /var/lib/botmail/dkim/public.pem
+
+# 4. Run
+java --enable-preview --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED \
+     -Djava.library.path=/opt/botmail/native/linux-x86_64 \
+     -jar /opt/botmail/botmail.jar \
+     --spring.config.location=file:/opt/botmail/application.properties
+```
+
+### JVM Arguments
+
+```
+--enable-preview                          # Java 22 preview features
+--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED        # FFM API access
+-Djava.library.path=<native-libs-dir>     # Native library search path
+-Xms512m -Xmx1024m                       # Heap sizing (adjust as needed)
+```
+
+### Required Ports
+
+| Port | Protocol | Service |
+|------|----------|---------|
+| 25 | TCP | SMTP (inbound/outbound) |
+| 8080 | TCP | HTTP API (behind Nginx) |
+| 8888 | TCP | HTCPCP server |
+| 25565 | TCP | Minecraft server |
+| Configurable | TCP | Honeypot traps |
+
+### DNS Records
+
+```
+MX    @               → 10 mail.yourdomain.com.
+A     mail            → <server-ip>
+TXT   @               → v=spf1 mx ~all
+TXT   _dmarc          → v=DMARC1; p=none;
+TXT   mail._domainkey → v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=<public-key-base64>
+```
+
+### Systemd Service
+
+```ini
+[Unit]
+Description=LmyzMail Application
+After=network.target postgresql.service redis.service
+
+[Service]
+User=botmail
+Group=botmail
+WorkingDirectory=/opt/botmail
+CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE CAP_BPF CAP_NET_ADMIN
+AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE CAP_BPF CAP_NET_ADMIN
+ExecStart=/usr/bin/java --enable-preview --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED \
+    -jar /opt/botmail/botmail.jar \
+    --spring.config.location=file:/opt/botmail/application.properties
+Restart=on-failure
+RestartSec=10
+
+[Install]
+WantedBy=multi-user.target
+```
+
+Note: `CAP_BPF` and `CAP_NET_ADMIN` are required for XDP firewall operation.
+
+## Verifying the Installation
+
+### Health Check
+
+```bash
+# SMTP banner test
+telnet localhost 25
+# Should see: 220 smtp-in.lmyz.net ESMTP ... Skibidi dop dop ...
+
+# HTTP API
+curl http://localhost:8080/api/status
+
+# HTCPCP test
+curl -X BREW http://localhost:8888/pot-0 \
+     -H "Content-Type: message/coffeepot" \
+     -d "start"
+```
+
+### Minecraft
+
+Connect with Minecraft 1.8.9 client to `yourserver:25565`.
+
