+# SMTP Server
+
+[← Back to Index](INDEX.md) | [← Getting Started](02-getting-started.md)
+
+## Overview
+
+LmyzMail implements a full RFC-compliant SMTP server built entirely on Netty, handling both inbound (receiving) and outbound (sending) email. The server is designed for high throughput with async I/O, connection pooling, and native transport (io_uring/epoll).
+
+## Inbound SMTP Server
+
+### Supported Commands
+
+| Command | RFC | Description |
+|---------|-----|-------------|
+| HELO | 5321 | Basic SMTP greeting |
+| EHLO | 5321 | Extended SMTP greeting with capability negotiation |
+| MAIL FROM | 5321 | Initiate mail transaction |
+| RCPT TO | 5321 | Specify recipient |
+| DATA | 5321 | Traditional message data transfer |
+| BDAT | 3030 | Chunked binary data transfer |
+| STARTTLS | 3207 | Upgrade to TLS |
+| AUTH | 4954 | SMTP authentication |
+| RSET | 5321 | Reset session |
+| VRFY | 5321 | Verify user (restricted) |
+| NOOP | 5321 | No operation |
+| QUIT | 5321 | Close connection |
+| HELP | 5321 | Help text |
+| SKIBIDITOILET | — | Custom: Brainrot quiz & ASCII video (see [Shitpost Features](04-shitpost-features.md)) |
+
+### SMTP Extensions (EHLO capabilities)
+
+| Extension | RFC | Config Key |
+|-----------|-----|-----------|
+| PIPELINING | 2920 | `botmail.smtp.pipelining-enabled` |
+| CHUNKING | 3030 | `botmail.smtp.chunking-enabled` |
+| 8BITMIME | 6152 | `botmail.smtp.eight-bit-mime-enabled` |
+| STARTTLS | 3207 | Always (when TLS available) |
+| ENHANCEDSTATUSCODES | 2034 | `botmail.smtp.enhanced-status-codes-enabled` |
+| SIZE | 1870 | Always (max email size) |
+| SMTPUTF8 | 6531 | Always |
+| SKIBIDITOILET | — | `botmail.smtp.skibidi-toilet-quiz-enabled` |
+
+### Connection Lifecycle
+
+```
+Client connects → TCP accept
+  │
+  ├─ Rate limit check (per-IP connections, new connections/min)
+  ├─ Spamhaus DNSBL check (if enabled)
+  ├─ XDP whitelist/blacklist check
+  │
+  ▼
+220 banner (with Skibidi expression from native generator or LM)
+  │
+  ├─ EHLO → Extension negotiation
+  ├─ STARTTLS → TLS upgrade (BoringSSL)
+  ├─ AUTH → Session authentication (for outbound relay)
+  ├─ MAIL FROM → SPF verification (parallel DNS query)
+  ├─ RCPT TO → Mailbox existence check
+  ├─ DATA/BDAT → Message content delivery
+  │     ├─ Content filter pipeline (spam scoring)
+  │     ├─ DKIM signature verification
+  │     ├─ DMARC policy evaluation
+  │     └─ Store to Maildir + PostgreSQL index
+  └─ QUIT → Close
+```
+
+### TLS Configuration
+
+The SMTP server uses netty-tcnative with BoringSSL for TLS:
+
+```properties
+botmail.ssl.use-custom-certificate=true
+botmail.ssl.keystore-path=/var/lib/botmail/ssl/lmyz.net.pfx
+botmail.ssl.keystore-password=<password>
+botmail.ssl.verify-server-certificate=true
+botmail.smtp.mta-sts-enabled=true
+```
+
+Supported: TLS 1.2/1.3 with modern cipher suites.
+
+### Email Verification Pipeline
+
+Each inbound email passes through multiple verification layers:
+
+1. **SPF Check** (`ParallelDnsQueryService`): Parallel DNS lookups for SPF record verification
+2. **DKIM Verification**: Signature validation using BouncyCastle
+3. **DMARC Policy**: Checks alignment between SPF/DKIM domains and From header, enforces domain policy
+4. **Content Filter** (`ContentSpamScanner`): Scoring-based pipeline with pluggable rules
+
+### Content Filter Rules
+
+| Rule | Category | Description |
+|------|----------|-------------|
+| `SpamKeywordDensityRule` | Body | High-density spam keyword detection |
+| `PhishingPatternRule` | Body | URL pattern analysis for phishing |
+| `SuspiciousUrlRule` | Body | Known malicious URL patterns |
+| `InvisibleTextRule` | Body | Hidden text tricks (white-on-white, font-size:0) |
+| `HtmlTextRatioRule` | Body | Excessive HTML vs visible text ratio |
+| `DangerousExtensionRule` | Attachment | .exe, .bat, .scr, etc. |
+| `DoubleExtensionRule` | Attachment | invoice.pdf.exe tricks |
+| `MimeTypeMismatchRule` | Attachment | Extension doesn't match MIME type |
+| `ExcessiveRecipientRule` | Header | Too many recipients (mass mail indicator) |
+| `FromReplyToMismatchRule` | Header | From/Reply-To domain mismatch |
+| `MissingRequiredHeaderRule` | Header | Missing Date, Message-ID, etc. |
+| `SubjectEncodingTrickRule` | Header | Unicode tricks in subject |
+| `SuspiciousDateRule` | Header | Future/past date anomalies |
+| `RblCheckRule` | Envelope | Real-time blacklist lookup |
+| `NewDomainRule` | Reputation | Recently registered domain detection |
+
+Each rule produces a weighted score. The aggregate determines the verdict:
+- **PASS**: Score below threshold → deliver normally
+- **SUSPECT**: Score in middle range → deliver with warning
+- **REJECT**: Score above threshold → reject with 5xx
+
+### SMTP Timeouts & Limits
+
+```properties
+botmail.smtp.connection-timeout-ms=120000
+botmail.smtp.command-timeout-ms=120000
+botmail.smtp.data-timeout-ms=300000
+botmail.smtp.max-messages-per-connection=10000
+botmail.smtp.max-recipients-per-message=100
+botmail.max-email-size-bytes=52428800       # 50MB
+botmail.max-attachment-size-bytes=50331648   # 48MB
+```
+
+## Outbound SMTP
+
+### Connection Pool
+
+The outbound system uses a high-performance connection pool:
+
+```properties
+botmail.outbound.pool-enabled=true
+botmail.outbound.max-connections-per-host=100
+botmail.outbound.max-messages-per-connection=1500
+botmail.outbound.max-idle-time-ms=30000
+botmail.outbound.connection-life-time-ms=300000
+botmail.outbound.pool-cleanup-interval-ms=1000
+```
+
+### Mail Queue
+
+Emails are persisted to PostgreSQL before delivery:
+
+```properties
+botmail.queue.batch-size=1200
+botmail.queue.max-concurrent-sends=400
+botmail.queue.poll-interval-ms=100
+botmail.queue.processing-timeout-minutes=10
+botmail.queue.sent-retention-days=7
+botmail.queue.failed-retention-days=30
+```
+
+Retry logic: Failed deliveries are retried up to `botmail.outbound.retryCount=3` times with exponential backoff.
+
+### DKIM Signing
+
+Outbound emails are signed with DKIM:
+
+```properties
+botmail.domains.main.dkimSelector=mail
+botmail.domains.main.dkimPrivateKeyPath=/var/lib/botmail/dkim/private.pem
+```
+
+The `DkimSigner` class handles RSA-SHA256 signing with relaxed/relaxed canonicalization.
+
+### MTA-STS Enforcement
+
+When `botmail.smtp.mta-sts-enabled=true`, the outbound system:
+1. Fetches the recipient domain's MTA-STS policy via HTTPS
+2. Validates the remote server's TLS certificate against the policy
+3. Refuses to deliver if the policy requires TLS and the server doesn't support it
+
+## Reporting
+
+### DMARC Aggregate Reports
+
+```properties
+botmail.reporting.enabled=true
+botmail.reporting.auto-send-enabled=true
+botmail.reporting.batch-size=500
+botmail.reporting.retention-days=90
+botmail.reporting.min-volume-for-report=10
+botmail.reporting.dmarc-report-sender-address=dmarc-reports-no-reply@lmyz.net
+botmail.reporting.organization-name=lmyzmail
+```
+
+The `DmarcReportGenerator` aggregates inbound DMARC verification results and generates XML reports per RFC 7489, delivering them to the addresses specified in recipient domains' DMARC records.
+
+### TLS-RPT Reports
+
+TLS reporting logs are maintained for outbound connections, tracking:
+- TLS negotiation success/failure
+- Certificate validation results
+- MTA-STS policy compliance
+
+Reports are generated and delivered per RFC 8460.
+
+## Protocol Detection & Mismatch Handling
+
+The SMTP server includes a `ProtocolMismatchDetector` that identifies when non-SMTP protocols (HTTP, SSH, etc.) connect to port 25. Instead of a cryptic error, it responds with protocol-appropriate mockery via `ProtocolMismatchResponder`.
+
+## DNS Caching
+
+The DNS subsystem uses a two-level cache:
+
+- **L1 (Caffeine)**: In-process, low-latency, configurable TTLs per record type
+- **L2 (Redis)**: Shared across instances, longer TTLs
+
+```properties
+botmail.dns.cache.enabled=true
+botmail.dns.cache.l1.max-size=10000
+botmail.dns.cache.l1.spf-ttl=10m
+botmail.dns.cache.l2.enabled=true
+botmail.dns.cache.l2.spf-ttl=30m
+```
+
+---
+
