+# Shitpost & Brainrot Features
+
+[← Back to Index](INDEX.md) | [← SMTP Server](03-smtp-server.md)
+
+## Philosophy
+
+LmyzMail embraces internet brainrot culture as both a humor feature and a security mechanism. Every shitpost element serves a dual purpose:
+
+1. **Entertainment**: Makes the server memorable and fun to interact with
+2. **Security**: Confuses automated scanners, wastes attacker time, and provides unique fingerprinting for IP reputation
+
+The brainrot vocabulary draws from Skibidi Toilet, Ohio memes, Sigma/Rizz culture, and general Gen-Z internet slang.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Skibidi SMTP Banner Generation
+
+Every SMTP connection greeting includes a randomized Skibidi expression.
+
+### How It Works
+
+When a client connects to port 25, the 220 banner includes a phrase like:
+```
+220 smtp-in.lmyz.net ESMTP Skibidi dop dop yes yes!
+220 smtp-in.lmyz.net ESMTP Brrrrr Skibidi dom dop dom dop!
+```
+
+### Generation Modes
+
+Controlled by `botmail.smtp.skibidi-generator-mode`:
+
+| Mode | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `NATIVE` | Uses the AVX2/AVX-512 optimized C library via FFM (fastest) |
+| `JAVA` | Pure Java fallback implementation |
+| `DISABLED` | Static expression only |
+
+### Native Generator (skibidi_generator)
+
+The native library (`libskibidi_avx.so`) generates expressions at microsecond latency:
+
+- **4-way parallel SIMD xorshift128+** random number generation
+- **AVX-512 memory operations** for buffer manipulation
+- **Cache-line aligned** state to prevent false sharing
+- **~26.85% fast-path probability** returns the canonical "Skibidi dop dop yes yes!" without FFM call
+
+Configuration:
+```properties
+botmail.smtp.skibidi-generator-mode=NATIVE
+botmail.smtp.skibidi-generator-enable-avx512=true
+botmail.smtp.skibidi-generator-enable-simd-rng=true
+```
+
+The expression format varies randomly:
+- Prefix: "Brrrrr " (probabilistic)
+- Core: "Skibidi " + combination of "dop"/"dom" syllables
+- Suffix: "yes yes!" / "!" (probabilistic)
+
+---
+
+## 2. SkibidiInferX LM — AI-Powered SMTP Rejection Messages
+
+When SPF verification fails (someone tries to spoof the server's domain), the rejection message is generated by a custom-trained 22M parameter transformer language model.
+
+### Architecture
+
+```
+SPF Failure Detected
+        │
+        ▼
+┌─────────────────────┐
+│  SkibidiInferxService│
+│  (Java)             │
+├─────────────────────┤
+│  BpeTokenizer       │ ← tokenizer.json (BPE vocabulary)
+│  TransformerRunner  │ ← Forward pass orchestration
+│  InferenceEngine    │ ← Model weights from .safetensors
+│  NativeOps (FFM)    │ ← SIMD-accelerated kernels
+└─────────────────────┘
+        │
+        ▼
+"5.7.1 Bro tried to impersonate our domain and caught the
+biggest L in SMTP history because the sigma SPF check said
+you have absolutely zero rizz no cap fr fr."
+```
+
+### Model Details
+
+- **Parameters**: ~22 million
+- **Architecture**: Decoder-only transformer (GPT-style) with SwiGLU FFN, RMSNorm
+- **Training data**: 25 prompt categories × ~200-1000 samples each, generated by Claude, GPT, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Qwen
+- **Format**: SafeTensors (`.safetensors`)
+- **Tokenizer**: BPE with custom vocabulary (`tokenizer.json`)
+
+### Native Inference Kernels
+
+The `skibidi_inferx_native` library provides SIMD-accelerated operations:
+
+| Operation | Description |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| `skibidi_matvec` | Matrix-vector multiply (y = Ax + b) |
+| `skibidi_rms_norm` | RMS normalization (no bias, eps=1e-6) |
+| `skibidi_silu_inplace` | SiLU activation for SwiGLU |
+| `skibidi_elementwise_mul` | Element-wise multiply for gating |
+| `skibidi_softmax_inplace` | Numerically stable softmax |
+| `skibidi_rope_inplace` | Rotary Position Embedding |
+| `skibidi_add_inplace` | Vector addition (residual connections) |
+
+Each operation has three implementations dispatched at runtime:
+- **AVX-512F** (fastest, if supported)
+- **AVX2 + FMA** (good fallback)
+- **Scalar** (universal compatibility)
+
+### Configuration
+
+```properties
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.enabled=true
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.model-path=classpath:skibidi-inferx-model/skibidi_ai.safetensors
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.tokenizer-path=classpath:skibidi-inferx-model/tokenizer.json
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.temperature=0.8
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.top-k=40
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.top-p=0.9
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.max-tokens=80
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.timeout-ms=1000
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.simd-level=auto          # auto|avx512|avx2|scalar
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.max-concurrent-generations=2
+botmail.skibidi-inferx.fallback-on-error=true
+```
+
+### Fallback Pool
+
+When the LM is disabled, times out, or errors, rejection messages come from a hardcoded pool:
+
+```
+5.7.1 L Rizz detected. You are not the Grimace Shake. Go back to Ohio.
+5.7.1 Erm, what the sigma? Blud really thought he could spoof this domain without paying the Fanum Tax.
+5.7.1 Skibidi dop dop NO NO. You have been mogged by the SPF record. Go mewing in Ohio.
+5.7.1 L + Ratio + Bozo + No Rizz + You're an NPC + Touch Grass. Your IP is literally cringe.
+```
+
+### Training Pipeline (`smtp-insult-ai/`)
+
+The `smtp-insult-ai/` directory contains the full ML training pipeline:
+
+| File | Purpose |
+|------|---------|
+| `training_data_prompt.md` | 25 different prompts used to generate training data |
+| `training_data_raw/prompt*/` | Raw training data from Claude, GPT, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Qwen |
+| `prompts.json` | Compiled prompt definitions |
+| `create_files.py` | Training data creation script |
+| `filter_dedup.py` | Deduplication and quality filtering |
+| `brainrot_filter.c` | Native C filter for byte-length validation (compiled to .exe) |
+| `tokenizer.py` | BPE tokenizer training |
+| `smtp_skibidi_ai_train.py` | Model training script |
+| `skibidi_inferx.py` | Python reference inference implementation |
+| `scripts/train.py` | Main training orchestration |
+| `scripts/wsl/` | WSL-specific training scripts |
+
+Training data categories include: SPF failure verdicts, "caught in 4k" narratives, Ohio energy readings, Sigma grindset evaluations, NPC dialogues, Fanum Tax invoices, and more.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Brainrot Quiz (SKIBIDITOILET SMTP Command)
+
+A fully playable quiz game accessible during an SMTP session.
+
+### Usage
+
+```
+C: SKIBIDITOILET HELP
+S: 250 Available commands: START, ANSWER, QUIT, WATCHSKIBIDITOILET
+
+C: SKIBIDITOILET START BABYGRONK
+S: 250 Quiz started! Level: BABY GRONK (15 questions)
+S: 250 Q1: What is the name of the series where toilets have cameras for heads?
+S: 250 A) Skibidi Toilet  B) Ohio Flush  C) Sigma Drain  D) Fanum Pipe
+
+C: SKIBIDITOILET ANSWER A
+S: 250 Correct! +10 points. Score: 10/100
+```
+
+### Difficulty Levels
+
+| Level | Name | Questions | Avg Difficulty | Description |
+|-------|------|-----------|---------------|-------------|
+| BABYGRONK | Baby Gronk | 15 | 4.0 | Easy mode, skewed toward simple questions |
+| SKIBIDITOILET | Skibidi Toilet | 30 | 5.0 | Balanced distribution |
+| OHIOFINALBOSS | Ohio Final Boss | 60 | 6.67 | Hard mode, heavy on difficulty 6-10 |
+
+### Question Selection Algorithm
+
+Questions are grouped into 10 difficulty buckets. Selection uses a weighted random algorithm with a greedy phase:
+
+1. Shuffle each bucket independently
+2. Pick questions using per-level bucket weights
+3. After `n - 5` questions, switch to greedy mode (target remaining difficulty budget)
+4. Guarantees no duplicates and accurate total difficulty targeting
+
+The question bank is loaded from `brainrot_quiz.json` at startup.
+
+---
+
+## 4. ASCII Art Video Streaming Over SMTP
+
+The `SKIBIDITOILET WATCHSKIBIDITOILET` command streams Skibidi Toilet Episode 1 as real-time ASCII art over the SMTP protocol.
+
+### How It Works
+
+```
+C: SKIBIDITOILET WATCHSKIBIDITOILET WIDTH=150 FPS=12 CONTRAST=1.4
+S: 250-[frame 1 ASCII art...]
+S: 250-[frame 2 ASCII art...]
+S: ...
+S: 250 PLAYBACK COMPLETE. Skibidi dop dop yes yes!
+```
+
+Each frame is sent as an SMTP multi-line response (250- prefix). The client sees ANSI-colored ASCII art animated at the configured frame rate.
+
+### Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Default | Description |
+|-----------|---------|-------------|
+| WIDTH | 150 | Character width of output |
+| FPS | 12 | Target frames per second |
+| CONTRAST | 1.4 | Contrast enhancement factor |
+| INVERT | false | Invert brightness |
+
+### Technical Implementation
+
+1. Video file (`skibidi_toilet_episode_1.mp4`) is bundled in the JAR
+2. `libasciiart.so` decodes video frames via FFmpeg and converts to ASCII using SIMD
+3. Playback runs on a dedicated platform thread (FFM pins virtual threads)
+4. ANSI escape sequences for cursor positioning and colors
+5. Backpressure handling: pauses if Netty channel is not writable
+
+Configuration:
+```properties
+botmail.smtp.asciiart.simd-mode=avx2     # auto|scalar|avx2|avx512
+botmail.smtp.asciiart.max-width=980
+botmail.smtp.asciiart.max-fps=30
+botmail.smtp.asciiart.default-width=150
+botmail.smtp.asciiart.default-fps=12
+botmail.smtp.asciiart.default-contrast=1.4
+botmail.smtp.asciiart.char-aspect=2.0
+```
+
+---
+
+## 5. Path Scan Trolling (SkibidiPathScanResponder)
+
+When vulnerability scanners probe common exploit paths on the HTTP server, instead of returning 404, the server returns **fake credentials and configs filled with brainrot** — formatted to look exactly like the real thing.
+
+### Supported Probe Paths
+
+The responder catches requests to paths like:
+- `/.env` → Fake environment variables with Skibidi passwords
+- `/wp-admin/` → Fake WordPress admin
+- `/phpMyAdmin/` → Fake database panel
+- `/.git/config` → Fake Git repository config
+- `/api/config` → Fake API configuration JSON
+- `/backup.sql` → Fake SQL dump
+- And many more common scanner targets
+
+### Example Output (for `/.env`)
+
+```env
+# Source: https://github.com/lmyzzzz/skibidi-dop-dop-engine/
+AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIA_SKIBIDI_TOILET_42069
+AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=SkibidiToiletSigmaGrindset42069RizzOhio
+DATABASE_URL=postgres://skibidi:Sk1b1d1T01l3t!2024@ohio-final-boss:5432/brainrot
+REDIS_PASSWORD=FanumT4x$Rizz99
+JWT_SECRET=sigma-grindset-activated-mewing-in-production-since-2024
+```
+
+### Design Goals
+
+1. **Waste attacker time**: They parse, store, and potentially try to use the fake credentials
+2. **Lure to GitHub**: Every response embeds links to the Skibidi Dop Dop Engine repository
+3. **Evade fingerprinting**: Values are randomized on each request
+4. **Score the IP**: Triggering this adds to the IP's "cringe score"
+
+---
+
+## 6. HTCPCP Server (RFC 2324 + RFC 7168)
+
+A fully RFC-compliant Hyper Text Coffee Pot Control Protocol server.
+
+### Supported Methods
+
+| Method | RFC | Description |
+|--------|-----|-------------|
+| BREW | 2324 §2.1.1 | Start/stop brewing |
+| POST | 2324 §2.1.1 | Equivalent to BREW |
+| GET | 2324 §2.1.2 | Query pot status |
+| PROPFIND | 2324 §2.1.3 | Discover brewed resource metadata |
+| WHEN | 2324 §2.1.4 | Signal "enough milk" |
+| HEAD | HTTP | Status without body |
+| OPTIONS | HTTP | Available methods |
+
+### Response Codes
+
+| Code | Meaning | When |
+|------|---------|------|
+| 200 | OK | Brew started/stopped successfully |
+| 300 | Multiple Choices | Tea variety selection needed |
+| 403 | Forbidden | Addition combination violates consensus |
+| 406 | Not Acceptable | Unsupported addition requested |
+| 418 | I'm a Teapot | Trying to brew coffee in a teapot |
+| 503 | Service Unavailable | Tea request on coffee-only pot |
+
+### Pot Configuration
+
+8 pots are configured with different capabilities:
+
+| Pot | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| pot-0 | Both | Dual-purpose workhorse |
+| pot-1 | Tea | East Asian purist (sweeteners only) |
+| pot-2 | Tea | British classic (milk and sugar) |
+| pot-3 | Coffee | Espresso machine (no alcohol) |
+| pot-4 | Coffee | Irish coffee (spirits + cream) |
+| pot-5 | Tea | Herbal sanctuary |
+| pot-6 | Coffee | Minimalist black (no additions) |
+| pot-7 | Both | Grand buffet (everything) |
+
+### Usage Example
+
+```bash
+# Brew coffee
+curl -X BREW http://server:8888/pot-0 \
+     -H "Content-Type: message/coffeepot" \
+     -H "Accept-Additions: Cream, Vanilla;amount=2" \
+     -d "start"
+
+# Query status
+curl http://server:8888/pot-0
+
+# Stop brewing
+curl -X BREW http://server:8888/pot-0 \
+     -H "Content-Type: message/coffeepot" \
+     -d "stop"
+
+# Brew tea (triggers 418 on coffee pot!)
+curl -X BREW http://server:8888/pot-6 \
+     -H "Content-Type: message/teapot" \
+     -d "start"
+# → 418 I'm a Teapot: "I am short and stout"
+```
+
+---
+
+## 7. Honeypot Mockery Responses
+
+The honeypot server doesn't just detect attackers — it mocks them in their own protocol language.
+
+### Protocol-Specific Insults
+
+| Protocol | Response Style |
+|----------|---------------|
+| SSH | Clown ASCII art + "Brain.exe not found" message |
+| HTTP | 25% 418 Teapot, 25% FBI redirect, 25% Rick Roll, 25% Skibidi |
+| FTP | Fake FTP banner with insult |
+| MySQL | Fake MySQL handshake |
+| Redis | Fake Redis response |
+| Minecraft | Valid SLP response with troll MOTD + skull favicon |
+| TLS | Certificate with insult in Subject/Organization fields |
+| RDP | TLS negotiation with mockery certificate |
+| VNC | Multi-step VNC auth handshake then mockery |
