+# Minecraft Email Server
+
+[← Back to Index](INDEX.md) | [← Shitpost Features](04-shitpost-features.md)
+
+## Overview
+
+LmyzMail includes a full Minecraft 1.8.9 (Protocol 47) server that allows players to compose, read, and send emails directly from within Minecraft. This is not a plugin for an existing server — it is a complete standalone protocol implementation built on Netty.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Full Protocol 47 implementation**: Handshake, Login, Play states
+- **Online-mode authentication**: Mojang session verification
+- **Email composition**: Write emails using Book & Quill
+- **Email reading**: Browse inbox via chest GUI with rendered email previews
+- **Video playback**: Watch videos on Minecraft map walls (ASCII art + map color matching)
+- **World template**: Pre-built mailroom world loaded from Anvil format regions
+- **Hologram text**: Floating text entities for instructions
+- **Scoreboard sidebar**: Session state display
+- **Compression**: Zlib packet compression above threshold
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+Minecraft 1.8.9 Client
+        │
+        ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  MinecraftChannelInitializer │
+│  VarIntFrameCodec            │ ← Length-prefixed framing
+│  PacketCodec                 │ ← Packet ID dispatch
+│  CompressionCodec            │ ← Zlib (after login)
+│  EncryptionCodec             │ ← AES/CFB8 (after auth)
+│  MinecraftSessionHandler     │ ← Game logic
+└─────────────────────────────┘
+        │
+        ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  PlayerSession               │
+│  ├─ PlayerState (FSM)        │
+│  ├─ DraftStore (email draft) │
+│  ├─ GuiManager (chest GUIs)  │
+│  └─ MapVideoPlayer           │
+└─────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+## Connection Flow
+
+1. **Handshake**: Client sends protocol version, server address, next state
+2. **Login**: Username exchange → Encryption request → Mojang auth verification → Login success
+3. **Play**: Join game → Chunk data → Spawn position → Player abilities → Hologram spawn
+
+## Player State Machine
+
+```
+HANDSHAKE → LOGIN → AWAITING_EMAIL → AWAITING_PASSWORD → AUTHENTICATED
+                                                              │
+                                                    (full email features)
+```
+
+After authentication (using their lmyzmail email + password), players can:
+- Compose emails (To, CC, BCC, Subject, Body)
+- Read inbox emails
+- Watch videos on the map wall
+
+## Email Composition
+
+### Writing Flow
+
+1. Player types their email address in chat → `AwaitingEmail` state
+2. Player types password → `AwaitingPassword` state → Session auth
+3. **Nether Star + Right-click** → Opens main menu (chest GUI)
+4. **Book & Quill** → Email body (multi-page support)
+5. **Sign buttons** (wall signs) → Set To, CC, BCC, Subject fields
+6. **Send button** → Queue email via `OutboundMailService`
+
+### GUI System
+
+The server uses chest inventories as GUIs:
+
+| GUI | Purpose |
+|-----|---------|
+| MainMenuGui | Central hub: Compose, Inbox, Video, Settings |
+| EmailListGui | Paginated inbox with rendered email previews |
+| MailViewManager | View individual emails with rendered content |
+| VideoMenuGui | Video playback controls |
+| ConfirmGui | Confirmation dialogs (send, delete) |
+
+Items in the GUI use custom NBT data (display names, lore) for interactivity.
+
+## Email Reading
+
+Inbox emails are displayed as a chest GUI with:
+- **Paper items**: Each represents one email (sender in name, subject in lore)
+- **Pagination**: Navigate through pages of emails
+- **View**: Click an email to see full content rendered on map wall
+
+### HTML Email Rendering
+
+When available, `libasciiart.so` with the mail render module converts HTML emails to Minecraft map tile data:
+
+1. HTML/CSS is parsed and rendered using litehtml (via native library)
+2. The rendered bitmap is converted to Minecraft map colors (128×128 per map)
+3. Map packets are sent to the player's client
+4. Maps are displayed on item frames forming a wall
+
+## Video Playback
+
+### ASCII Art Video Wall
+
+Videos can be played as block-art on a wall in the Minecraft world:
+- Each frame is converted to colored blocks using palette matching
+- Blocks are placed/updated in real-time at the configured FPS
+- Uses SIMD-accelerated color matching (AVX2/AVX-512)
+
+### Map Video Wall
+
+A more advanced video display using Minecraft maps:
+- Videos decoded via FFmpeg (through `libasciiart.so`)
+- Each frame is color-matched to Minecraft's map palette
+- Frames are sent as map data packets to players
+- Configuration defines wall dimensions (maps × maps)
+
+```properties
+botmail.minecraft.video.center-x=0
+botmail.minecraft.video.center-y=160
+botmail.minecraft.video.wall-z=-50
+botmail.minecraft.video.max-width=240
+botmail.minecraft.video.max-fps=20
+
+botmail.minecraft.map-video.center-x=-1
+botmail.minecraft.map-video.center-y=163
+botmail.minecraft.map-video.center-z=-6
+botmail.minecraft.map-video.facing=SOUTH
+botmail.minecraft.map-video.max-maps-x=10
+botmail.minecraft.map-video.max-maps-y=10
+```
+
+## World System
+
+### World Template
+
+The server loads a pre-built world from Anvil region files:
+```
+src/main/resources/worlds/mailroom/region/
+├── r.-1.-1.mca
+├── r.-1.0.mca
+├── r.0.-1.mca
+└── r.0.0.mca
+```
+
+The `AnvilLoader` reads these files and the `ChunkSerializer` converts them to Protocol 47 chunk data packets.
+
+### Spawn Protection
+
+Players are kept within `maxSpawnDistance` blocks of spawn. If they wander too far, they're teleported back.
+
+## Configuration
+
+```properties
+# Master switch
+botmail.minecraft.enabled=true
+botmail.minecraft.port=25565
+
+# Authentication
+botmail.minecraft.online-mode=true          # Mojang auth (false = offline/cracked)
+botmail.minecraft.max-players=5
+
+# Display
+botmail.minecraft.motd=§6LMYZMAIL §7- Send skibidi emails in Minecraft
+botmail.minecraft.compression-threshold=256
+
+# Networking
+botmail.minecraft.boss-threads=1
+botmail.minecraft.worker-threads=0           # 0 = auto (CPU cores × 2)
+botmail.minecraft.keep-alive-interval-seconds=15
+botmail.minecraft.read-timeout-seconds=30
+
+# World
+botmail.minecraft.world-template=worlds/mailroom
+botmail.minecraft.view-distance=32           # Chunks to send around spawn
+botmail.minecraft.max-spawn-distance=100     # Blocks before teleport-back
+
+# Performance
+botmail.minecraft.max-concurrent-videos=2    # Limit decode sessions
+```
+
+### Access Control
+
+```properties
+# Whitelist mode
+botmail.minecraft.whitelist.enabled=false
+botmail.minecraft.whitelist.players[0]=AllowedPlayer
+
+# Blacklist
+botmail.minecraft.blacklist.players[0]=BannedPlayer
+```
+
+### Hologram Configuration
+
+Floating text displayed to players:
+
+```properties
+botmail.minecraft.hologram.x=0.5
+botmail.minecraft.hologram.y=162.0
+botmail.minecraft.hologram.z=-3.5
+botmail.minecraft.hologram.lines[0]=§6§l=== LMYZMAIL ===
+botmail.minecraft.hologram.lines[1]=§eSend Real Emails from Minecraft 1.8.9
+botmail.minecraft.hologram.lines[7]=§eHold §fNether Star §e+ Right-click -> §fMenu
+botmail.minecraft.hologram.lines[8]=§eWrite in §fBook & Quill §e-> Email body
+```
+
+## Email Signature
+
+All emails sent from Minecraft automatically include:
+```
+--- Sent with lmyzmail from Minecraft 1.8.9 ---
+```
+
+## Security
+
+- **Rate limiting**: `MinecraftAuthLimiter` prevents brute-force auth attempts
+- **Connection limit**: Max players enforced
+- **Cringe scoring**: Failed auth attempts from Minecraft contribute to IP reputation
+- **Online mode**: Mojang session verification prevents impersonation
+
+---
+
