+# Native Libraries & SIMD Acceleration
+
+[← Back to Index](INDEX.md) | [← Minecraft Server](05-minecraft-server.md)
+
+## Overview
+
+LmyzMail uses four native C libraries accessed via Java 22's Foreign Function & Memory (FFM) API (Project Panama). All libraries feature runtime SIMD capability detection and multi-level dispatch (AVX-512 → AVX2 → Scalar).
+
+## 1. Skibidi Generator (`skibidi_generator/`)
+
+**Purpose**: Ultra-fast random "Skibidi dop dop" expression generation for SMTP banners.
+
+### Files
+
+| File | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `skibidi_avx.h` | Public API header |
+| `skibidi_avx.c` | Implementation (850+ lines) |
+| `build_native.sh` | Linux build script |
+| `build.ps1` | Windows build script |
+
+### API Functions
+
+```c
+// Initialize the library (detects CPU capabilities)
+int skibidi_init(void);
+
+// Configure behavior
+int skibidi_configure(int enable_avx512, int enable_simd_rng);
+
+// Generate a single expression
+int skibidi_generate(char* buffer, size_t buffer_size, size_t* out_length);
+
+// Batch generate multiple expressions
+int skibidi_generate_batch(char** buffers, size_t buffer_size, 
+                           size_t* out_lengths, int count);
+
+// Query CPU capabilities
+uint32_t skibidi_get_cpu_caps(void);
+```
+
+### SIMD Features
+
+- **xorshift128+ SIMD RNG**: 4-way parallel random number generation using AVX2 256-bit registers
+- **AVX-512 memory operations**: 512-bit store operations for buffer initialization
+- **Cache-line alignment**: All state structures aligned to 64-byte boundaries to prevent false sharing
+- **CPUID detection**: Runtime detection of SSE2, AVX, AVX2, AVX-512F/VL/BW/DQ
+
+### Expression Grammar
+
+```
+expression = [prefix] "Skibidi " syllables [suffix]
+prefix     = "Brrrrr " (probabilistic)
+syllables  = ("dop" | "dom"){2-5}
+suffix     = " yes yes!" | "!" (probabilistic)
+```
+
+### Performance
+
+From `skibidi_bench/`:
+- Native AVX2: ~100ns per expression
+- Native Scalar: ~200ns per expression
+- Java fallback: ~500ns per expression
+
+### Java Binding (`SkibidiNativeService`)
+
+Uses Java 22 FFM confined arenas for zero-copy buffer management:
+
+```java
+try (Arena arena = Arena.ofConfined()) {
+    MemorySegment buffer = arena.allocate(SKIBIDI_MIN_BUFFER_SIZE);
+    MemorySegment outLen = arena.allocate(ValueLayout.JAVA_LONG);
+    int result = (int) generateHandle.invokeExact(buffer, (long) SKIBIDI_MIN_BUFFER_SIZE, outLen);
+    return buffer.getString(0, StandardCharsets.US_ASCII);
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## 2. SkibidiInferX Native (`skibidi_inferx_native/`)
+
+**Purpose**: SIMD-accelerated transformer inference kernels for the brainrot text generation LM.
+
+### Directory Structure
+
+```
+skibidi_inferx_native/
+├── native_linux/
+│   ├── include/
+│   │   ├── skibidi_native.h      # Public API
+│   │   └── kernels.h             # Internal kernel declarations
+│   ├── src/
+│   │   ├── dispatch.c            # Runtime function dispatch
+│   │   ├── simd_detect.c         # CPUID capability detection
+│   │   ├── kernels_scalar.c      # Scalar fallback implementations
+│   │   ├── kernels_avx2.c        # AVX2+FMA optimized kernels
+│   │   └── kernels_avx512.c      # AVX-512 optimized kernels
+│   ├── CMakeLists.txt
+│   ├── build.sh
+│   └── build.cmd
+└── native_win/                    # Windows equivalent
+```
+
+### API Functions
+
+```c
+// Initialize with auto-detection
+int skibidi_init(void);                    // Returns: 0=Scalar, 1=AVX2, 2=AVX-512
+
+// Initialize with forced level
+int skibidi_init_with_level(int max_level); // -1=auto, 0=scalar, 1=avx2, 2=avx512
+
+// Matrix-vector multiply: y = A*x + bias
+void skibidi_matvec(const float* A, const float* x, const float* bias,
+                    float* y, int rows, int cols);
+
+// RMS Normalization
+void skibidi_rms_norm(const float* in, const float* weight,
+                      float* out, int size, float eps);
+
+// SiLU activation (in-place)
+void skibidi_silu_inplace(float* x, int size);
+
+// Element-wise multiply (for SwiGLU gating)
+void skibidi_elementwise_mul(float* dst, const float* src, int size);
+
+// Softmax (numerically stable, in-place)
+void skibidi_softmax_inplace(float* x, int size);
+
+// Rotary Position Embedding (in-place)
+void skibidi_rope_inplace(float* q, float* k, int dim, int head_dim,
+                          int n_heads, int pos);
+
+// Vector addition (residual connections)
+void skibidi_add_inplace(float* dst, const float* src, int size);
+```
+
+### Dispatch Mechanism
+
+```c
+// Function pointer table (set during init)
+static void (*matvec_fn)(const float*, const float*, const float*, float*, int, int);
+
+int skibidi_init(void) {
+    int level = detect_simd_level();
+    switch (level) {
+        case 2: matvec_fn = matvec_avx512; break;
+        case 1: matvec_fn = matvec_avx2;   break;
+        default: matvec_fn = matvec_scalar; break;
+    }
+    return level;
+}
+```
+
+### Java Integration (`skibidi_inferx/` package)
+
+| Class | Purpose |
+|-------|---------|
+| `NativeLibLoader` | Extracts and loads the platform-specific .so/.dll |
+| `NativeOps` | FFM method handle bindings for all native functions |
+| `ModelWeights` | Loads SafeTensors format, mmaps weight tensors |
+| `BpeTokenizer` | BPE tokenization (encode text → token IDs) |
+| `InferenceEngine` | Orchestrates the full forward pass |
+| `TransformerRunner` | Layer-by-layer execution with KV cache |
+| `KvCache` | Key-Value cache for autoregressive generation |
+| `Sampler` | Temperature, Top-K, Top-P sampling |
+
+### Model Architecture (inferred from code)
+
+- Decoder-only transformer
+- RMSNorm (no LayerNorm bias)
+- SwiGLU FFN (SiLU gate × up projection)
+- Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE)
+- ~22M parameters total
+
+---
+
+## 3. ASCII Art Library (`asciiart_linux/`)
+
+**Purpose**: Video decoding and conversion to ASCII art or Minecraft map colors.
+
+### Modules
+
+| Module | Files | Purpose |
+|--------|-------|---------|
+| ASCII Art Core | `aa_*.c` | Video → text-based ASCII art |
+| Minecraft Color | `mc_*.c` | Video → Minecraft block palette matching |
+| Minecraft Map | `mc_map_*.c` | Video → Minecraft map color palette |
+| Mail Render | `mr_*.cpp` | HTML email → bitmap (via litehtml + Cairo) |
+
+### Core API (`asciiart.h`)
+
+```c
+// Create/destroy context
+aa_context* aa_create(aa_config* config);
+void aa_destroy(aa_context* ctx);
+
+// Open video file
+int aa_open_video(aa_context* ctx, const char* path);
+
+// Decode next frame to ASCII
+int aa_next_frame(aa_context* ctx, char* buffer, size_t buffer_size, size_t* out_len);
+
+// Get frame timing
+double aa_get_frame_time(aa_context* ctx);
+```
+
+### SIMD Implementations
+
+Each conversion module has three implementations:
+
+| Level | ASCII Art | MC Colors | MC Map |
+|-------|-----------|-----------|--------|
+| Scalar | `aa_convert_scalar.c` | `mc_match_scalar.c` | `mc_map_match_scalar.c` |
+| AVX2 | `aa_convert_avx2.c` | `mc_match_avx2.c` | `mc_map_match_avx2.c` |
+| AVX-512 | `aa_convert_avx512.c` | `mc_match_avx512.c` | `mc_map_match_avx512.c` |
+
+The color matching uses a nearest-neighbor search in RGB space. SIMD parallelizes the distance computation across multiple palette entries simultaneously.
+
+### Mail Render Module
+
+```cpp
+// mr_render.cpp - Renders HTML to bitmap using litehtml + Cairo
+// mr_container.cpp - litehtml document container implementation
+```
+
+Dependencies: litehtml, Cairo, FreeType, libpng, Pixman (all statically linked from `static_deps/`).
+
+### Build Configuration
+
+```cmake
+option(AA_BUILD_TESTS    "Build test programs"    ON)
+option(AA_BUILD_EXAMPLES "Build example programs" ON)
+option(AA_STATIC_FFMPEG  "Statically link FFmpeg" OFF)
+option(MR_BUILD_MAIL_RENDER "Build mail render module" OFF)
+```
+
+### Java Bindings
+
+| Java Class | Native Module |
+|-----------|---------------|
+| `AsciiArtLibrary` | aa_* functions |
+| `AsciiArtContext` | Context lifecycle |
+| `AsciiArtVideo` | Video playback |
+| `McArtLibrary` | mc_* functions (block palette) |
+| `McArtVideo` | Minecraft block video |
+| `McMapLibrary` | mc_map_* functions |
+| `McMapVideoDecoder` | Map color video |
+| `MailRenderLibrary` | mr_* functions |
+| `MailRenderer` | High-level HTML→map render |
+
+---
+
+## 4. XDP Firewall (`lmyzmail-xdp/`)
+
+**Purpose**: Kernel-level packet filtering using eBPF/XDP for million-PPS DoS mitigation.
+
+### Components
+
+| File | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `bpf/xdp_firewall.bpf.c` | eBPF program (runs in kernel) |
+| `src/xdp_firewall.c` | Userspace library (loads/manages BPF) |
+| `src/xdp_firewall.h` | Public API |
+| `Makefile` | Build system |
+| `build.sh` | Build convenience script |
+
+### BPF Maps
+
+| Map | Type | Purpose |
+|-----|------|---------|
+| blocked_ips_v4 | Hash | IPv4 ban list (100K entries) |
+| blocked_ips_v6 | Hash | IPv6 ban list |
+| whitelist_v4 | LPM Trie | IPv4 CIDR whitelist (10K entries) |
+| whitelist_v6 | LPM Trie | IPv6 CIDR whitelist |
+| stats | Per-CPU Array | Packet counters (passed/dropped/total/SYN) |
+
+### Userspace API
+
+```c
+// Lifecycle
+int xdp_fw_init(const char* bpf_obj_path, const char* iface, const char* pin_path);
+void xdp_fw_cleanup(void);
+
+// IP management
+int xdp_fw_ban_ipv4(uint32_t addr, uint32_t reason);
+int xdp_fw_unban_ipv4(uint32_t addr);
+int xdp_fw_whitelist_ipv4(uint32_t addr, uint32_t prefix_len);
+
+// Statistics
+int xdp_fw_get_stats(uint64_t* passed, uint64_t* dropped, uint64_t* total);
+```
+
+### Java Integration (`XdpFirewall`, `XdpFirewallService`)
+
+The Java layer uses FFM to call the native library and manages:
+- Automatic sync of high-score IPs from PostgreSQL to XDP on startup
+- Dynamic ban/unban based on cringe score thresholds
+- PPS monitoring via `XdpPpsMonitorService`
+
+---
+
+## FFM (Foreign Function & Memory) Usage Pattern
+
+All native bindings follow this pattern:
+
+```java
+// 1. Library loading
+static {
+    Linker linker = Linker.nativeLinker();
+    SymbolLookup lib = SymbolLookup.libraryLookup("libname.so", Arena.global());
+    
+    // 2. Method handle creation
+    MethodHandle initHandle = linker.downcallHandle(
+        lib.find("skibidi_init").orElseThrow(),
+        FunctionDescriptor.of(ValueLayout.JAVA_INT)
+    );
+}
+
+// 3. Invocation (confined arena for temp buffers)
+try (Arena arena = Arena.ofConfined()) {
+    MemorySegment buffer = arena.allocate(size);
+    int result = (int) handle.invokeExact(buffer, size);
+}
+```
+
+Key consideration: FFM downcalls pin virtual threads to their carrier platform thread. All native-heavy work runs on dedicated platform thread executors, not virtual threads.
+
