+# Security & Firewall
+
+[← Back to Index](INDEX.md) | [← Native Libraries](06-native-libraries.md)
+
+## Security Architecture
+
+LmyzMail implements defense-in-depth with multiple layers:
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│  Layer 1: XDP Firewall (Kernel Space)            │
+│  - Drops banned IPs at NIC driver level          │
+│  - Millions of PPS capacity                      │
+│  - CIDR whitelist bypass                         │
+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│  Layer 2: Connection Limits (Netty)              │
+│  - Per-IP concurrent connection caps             │
+│  - New connection rate limits                    │
+│  - Idle timeout enforcement                      │
+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│  Layer 3: SMTP Security                          │
+│  - Tarpitting (exponential delay)                │
+│  - Spamhaus DNSBL lookup                         │
+│  - Command count limits                          │
+│  - Auth failure tracking                         │
+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│  Layer 4: Email Verification                     │
+│  - SPF / DKIM / DMARC                           │
+│  - Content filtering (spam rules)                │
+│  - Rate limiting (per-account)                   │
+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│  Layer 5: Application Security                   │
+│  - API key authentication                        │
+│  - Session management                            │
+│  - CORS enforcement                              │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+---
+
+## 1. XDP Firewall
+
+### What Is XDP?
+
+eXpress Data Path (XDP) is a Linux kernel technology that executes eBPF programs at the earliest point in the network stack — before the kernel allocates sk_buff structures. This allows packet processing at millions of packets per second with near-zero CPU overhead.
+
+### How LmyzMail Uses XDP
+
+The XDP firewall (`lmyzmail-xdp/`) maintains kernel-space hash maps of banned IPs. When a packet arrives from a banned IP, it is dropped instantly at the NIC driver level without ever reaching userspace.
+
+### Configuration
+
+```properties
+# Enable XDP firewall
+botmail.xdp.enabled=true
+
+# Network interface
+botmail.xdp.interface-name=eth0
+
+# BPF object file (auto-discovered if empty)
+botmail.xdp.bpf-object-path=
+
+# Map pinning path
+botmail.xdp.pin-path=/sys/fs/bpf/botmail
+
+# Score thresholds
+botmail.xdp.ban-threshold=80       # Ban when score >= 80
+botmail.xdp.unban-threshold=64     # Unban when score < 64
+
+# Mode
+botmail.xdp.force-generic-mode=false   # true = SKB mode (slower but more compatible)
+botmail.xdp.verbose=true
+botmail.xdp.sync-on-startup=true       # Load bans from DB on startup
+```
+
+### Whitelist
+
+IPs/CIDRs that should never be banned (checked via LPM Trie in kernel):
+
+```properties
+botmail.xdp.whitelist=\
+  127.0.0.1,\
+  ::1,\
+  10.0.0.0/8,\
+  192.168.0.0/16,\
+  74.125.0.0/16,\         # Google
+  209.85.128.0/17,\       # Google
+  2001:4860:4000::/36,\   # Google IPv6
+  ...
+```
+
+### Statistics
+
+The BPF program tracks per-CPU counters:
+- Total packets processed
+- Packets dropped (banned IPs)
+- Packets passed
+- TCP SYN packets (for SYN flood detection)
+- Whitelisted packets
+
+`XdpPpsMonitorService` polls these counters for monitoring.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Cringe Score System
+
+The "Skibidi Cringe IP" system is a reputation scoring mechanism that tracks malicious behavior per IP address.
+
+### How It Works
+
+```
+Malicious Activity Detected
+        │
+        ▼
+┌─────────────────────┐
+│  SkibidiCringeIPService │
+│  - Add score points      │
+│  - Check thresholds      │
+└──────────┬──────────┘
+           │
+    score >= ban_threshold?
+           │
+     ┌─────┴─────┐
+     │ YES       │ NO
+     ▼           ▼
+┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐
+│ XDP Ban  │  │  Continue │
+│ (kernel) │  │  monitoring│
+└──────────┘  └──────────┘
+```
+
+### Activity Types (`SkibidiCringeActivityType`)
+
+Each activity adds a configurable number of points:
+
+| Activity | Description |
+|----------|-------------|
+| SMTP error patterns | Repeated SMTP failures |
+| Auth failures | Wrong password attempts |
+| Port scanning | Connecting to honeypot ports |
+| Protocol mismatch | Non-SMTP on port 25 |
+| Spamhaus listed | IP found in DNSBL |
+| Rate limit exceeded | Sending too fast |
+| Invalid commands | SMTP command abuse |
+| Vulnerability scanning | Probing exploit paths |
+
+### Score Decay
+
+A scheduled task (`SkibidiCringeDecayScheduler`) gradually reduces scores over time, allowing temporarily misbehaving IPs to recover:
+
+```properties
+# Decay configuration (in CringeDecayProperties)
+# Points decayed per cycle
+# Cycle interval
+```
+
+### Batch Writing
+
+To handle high-throughput score updates without overwhelming the database, `CringeBatchWriteService` batches writes:
+- Accumulates score changes in memory
+- Flushes to PostgreSQL periodically
+- Handles concurrent access safely
+
+### XDP Sync
+
+`XdpCringeSyncService` synchronizes the cringe score database with the XDP firewall:
+- On startup: loads all IPs above threshold into XDP ban map
+- On score change: immediately updates XDP if crossing threshold
+- On decay: removes from XDP if score drops below unban threshold
+
+---
+
+## 3. Multi-Protocol Honeypot
+
+### Supported Detection Protocols
+
+| Protocol | Detection Method |
+|----------|-----------------|
+| SMTP | Command pattern matching |
+| SSH | Version string prefix |
+| FTP | Command set |
+| MySQL | Capability flags packet |
+| POP3 | Command pattern |
+| IMAP | Command pattern |
+| HTTP | Method + headers |
+| Redis | RESP protocol |
+| Memcached | Binary/text protocol |
+| MongoDB | Wire protocol header |
+| PostgreSQL | Startup message |
+| SOCKS4/5 | Version byte |
+| TLS/SSL | ClientHello record |
+| Minecraft | VarInt handshake packet |
+| RDP | TPKT header + X.224 |
+| Zabbix | Agent protocol |
+| VNC | Version negotiation |
+
+### Trap Configuration
+
+Each honeypot trap is defined with:
+- **Port**: Which port to listen on
+- **Server Protocol**: What to pretend to be (banner to send)
+- **Label**: Human-readable name for logging
+
+### Behavior
+
+1. Connection arrives at honeypot port
+2. Short delay (configurable) to see if client speaks first
+3. If client silent → send server banner (mimicking configured protocol)
+4. Detect actual client protocol from their first bytes
+5. Respond with protocol-appropriate mockery
+6. Record activity → add cringe score → close connection
+
+### Logging Strategy
+
+Inspired by Tomcat's log throttling:
+- First hit from an IP: INFO-level log
+- Subsequent hits within 1 hour: DEBUG-level
+- After 1 hour: INFO again with accumulated statistics
+
+---
+
+## 4. SMTP Security
+
+### Tarpitting
+
+Intentionally delays responses to misbehaving clients:
+
+```properties
+botmail.smtp-security.tarpit-enabled=true
+botmail.smtp-security.tarpit-base-delay-ms=500
+botmail.smtp-security.tarpit-max-delay-ms=20000
+botmail.smtp-security.tarpit-error-threshold=10
+botmail.smtp-security.tarpit-multiplier=1.5
+botmail.smtp-security.tarpit-banned-ip-delay-ms=8000
+```
+
+Delay formula: `min(base × multiplier^(errors - threshold), max_delay)`
+
+### Spamhaus DNSBL
+
+```properties
+botmail.smtp-security.spamhaus-enabled=true
+botmail.smtp-security.spamhaus-zones[0]=zen.spamhaus.org
+botmail.smtp-security.spamhaus-reject-on-listed=true
+botmail.smtp-security.spamhaus-timeout-ms=5000
+botmail.smtp-security.spamhaus-cache-ttl-seconds=600
+botmail.smtp-security.spamhaus-dbl-enabled=true
+botmail.smtp-security.spamhaus-dbl-zone=dbl.spamhaus.org
+```
+
+PBL (Policy Block List) codes can be ignored to allow legitimate dynamic IP servers.
+
+### Connection Limits
+
+```properties
+botmail.smtp-security.connection-limits-enabled=true
+botmail.smtp-security.max-connections-per-ip=200
+botmail.smtp-security.max-new-connections-per-minute-per-ip=200
+botmail.smtp-security.max-commands-per-connection=6000
+botmail.smtp-security.max-errors-per-connection=15
+botmail.smtp-security.max-rcpt-per-connection=100
+```
+
+### Slowloris Protection
+
+```properties
+botmail.smtp-security.command-timeout-ms=120000
+botmail.smtp-security.max-connection-duration-ms=600000
+botmail.smtp-security.max-idle-time-ms=120000
+```
+
+---
+
+## 5. Rate Limiting
+
+### SMTP Rate Limits
+
+```properties
+botmail.rate-limit.smtp-rate-limit-enabled=false
+botmail.rate-limit.smtp-max-errors-per-ip-per-hour=100
+botmail.rate-limit.smtp-block-duration-minutes=15
+botmail.rate-limit.smtp-max-auth-failures-per-hour=20
+botmail.rate-limit.smtp-auto-ban-enabled=true
+botmail.rate-limit.smtp-auto-ban-threshold=200
