+│  └────┬─────┘  └────┬─────┘  └──────┬───────┘                       │
+│       │              │               │                               │
+│       ▼              ▼               ▼                               │
+│  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────────────────┐               │
+│  │PostgreSQL│  │  Redis   │  │ libskibidi_avx.so    │               │
+│  │  (JPA)   │  │ (Cache)  │  │ libskibidi_inferx.so │               │
+│  └──────────┘  └──────────┘  │ libasciiart.so       │               │
+│                               │ liblmyzmail_xdp.so   │               │
+│                               └──────────────────────┘               │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+         │
+         ▼
+┌─────────────────────┐
+│  XDP/eBPF Firewall  │
+│  (kernel-level)     │
+└─────────────────────┘
+```
+
+## Module Overview
+
+### Core Email Modules
+
+| Package | Purpose |
+|---------|---------|
+| `inbound/` | SMTP inbound: Netty-based server, SPF/DKIM/DMARC verification, DNS caching, tarpitting |
+| `outbound/` | SMTP outbound: DKIM signing, connection pooling, MX resolution, retry queue |
+| `mailbox/` | Mail storage (Maildir), email index, REST API for mail operations |
+| `contentfilter/` | Pluggable spam rule pipeline (scoring-based verdict) |
+| `report/` | DMARC aggregate report and TLS-RPT generation/delivery |
+
+### Netty Server Modules
+
+| Package | Purpose |
+|---------|---------|
+| `netty/smtp/` | Full SMTP server: commands, STARTTLS, PIPELINING, BDAT, quiz, video |
+| `netty/http/` | Custom annotation-driven HTTP framework on Netty (replaces Tomcat) |
+| `netty/minecraft/` | Minecraft 1.8.9 (protocol 47) email client server |
+| `netty/htcpcp/` | RFC 2324 + RFC 7168 Hyper Text Coffee Pot Control Protocol |
+| `netty/honeypot/` | Multi-protocol honeypot with mockery responses |
+
+### Native Integration Modules
+
+| Package | Purpose |
+|---------|---------|
+| `asciiart/` | FFM bindings for libasciiart (video→ASCII, video→Minecraft maps) |
+| `skibidi_inferx/` | Transformer LM inference engine (tokenizer, sampling, KV cache) |
+| `util/native_/` | Skibidi expression generator, XDP firewall JNI, native lib loader |
+
+### Security & Reputation Modules
+
+| Package | Purpose |
+|---------|---------|
+| `cringe/` | IP reputation scoring system with XDP sync |
+| `ratelimit/` | Rate limiting (per-account, per-IP, SMTP-level) |
+| `session/` | Session management with Redis-backed tracking |
+
+## Threading Model
+
+LmyzMail uses a hybrid threading approach:
+
+1. **Netty EventLoops**: All network I/O (SMTP, HTTP, Minecraft, HTCPCP, Honeypot) runs on Netty EventLoops using the best available transport (io_uring > epoll > NIO, auto-detected).
+
+2. **Virtual Threads** (Java 21+): Blocking operations (database queries, DNS lookups, Mojang auth) run on virtual threads via `spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true`.
+
+3. **Platform Thread Executors**: FFM-heavy work (video decode, native inference) runs on dedicated platform thread pools because Foreign Function downcalls pin virtual threads.
+
+4. **XDP/eBPF**: Packet filtering runs in kernel space at NIC driver level, completely bypassing the userspace TCP/IP stack.
+
+## Data Flow: Inbound Email
+
+```
+Internet → [XDP Firewall] → TCP:25 → Netty SMTP Pipeline
+    │
+    ├─ EHLO/HELO → Skibidi banner (native gen or LM inference)
+    ├─ STARTTLS → BoringSSL via netty-tcnative
+    ├─ MAIL FROM → SPF check (parallel DNS)
+    ├─ RCPT TO → Local mailbox validation
+    ├─ DATA/BDAT → Content filter pipeline
+    │   ├─ Header rules (encoding tricks, date anomalies)
+    │   ├─ Body rules (phishing URLs, spam keywords, invisible text)
+    │   ├─ Attachment rules (double extensions, MIME mismatch)
+    │   └─ Reputation rules (RBL, new domain)
+    ├─ Score aggregation → Accept / Reject / Quarantine
+    ├─ DKIM verification
+    ├─ DMARC policy check
+    └─ Store to Maildir + index in PostgreSQL
+```
+
+## Data Flow: Outbound Email
+
+```
+API/Minecraft Client → OutboundMailService
+    │
+    ├─ DKIM signing (RSA-SHA256, ed25519)
+    ├─ Enqueue to PostgreSQL (persistent queue)
+    ├─ MailQueueScheduler polls queue
+    ├─ MX resolution (with DNS cache L1/L2)
+    ├─ SmtpConnectionPool (per-host pooling)
+    ├─ MTA-STS policy enforcement
+    ├─ TLS negotiation (STARTTLS / implicit)
+    └─ Delivery + TLS-RPT logging
+```
+
+## Configuration Architecture
+
+The application uses Spring Boot's `@ConfigurationProperties` pattern extensively:
+
+- `BotmailProperties` — Top-level config (domains, DKIM, storage, HTCPCP)
+- `SmtpProperties` — SMTP server settings (port, extensions, timeouts)
+- `SmtpSecurityProperties` — Security settings (tarpitting, DNSBL, connection limits)
+- `SkibidiInferxProperties` — AI inference engine settings
+- `MinecraftProperties` — Minecraft server configuration
+- `HoneypotProperties` — Honeypot trap definitions
+- `XdpProperties` — XDP firewall settings
+- `DnsCacheProperties` — L1 (Caffeine) + L2 (Redis) DNS cache
+- `RateLimitProperties` — Rate limiting thresholds
+- `ContentFilterProperties` — Spam filter rule weights and thresholds
+
+## Key Design Decisions
+
+1. **No Tomcat/Servlet**: The entire HTTP layer is a custom Netty-based framework (`netty/http/`) using annotations like `@NettyController`, `@GetMapping`, `@PostMapping`. Spring's web starter is present only for validation beans.
+
+2. **`spring.main.web-application-type=none`**: Disables the Servlet container entirely; all servers are Netty bootstrap instances managed by Spring lifecycle.
+
+3. **Native-first performance**: Hot paths (SMTP banner generation, AI inference, video transcoding, XDP firewall) use native C code accessed via Java 22 FFM API with SIMD acceleration.
+
+4. **Single JAR deployment**: Native libraries (`.so`, `.dll`) and model files (`.safetensors`) are packaged inside the boot JAR and extracted at runtime.
+
+5. **Humor as a feature**: Brainrot/shitpost elements are not cosmetic — they serve security purposes (confusing scanners, wasting attacker time, IP reputation scoring).
+
