+## Deployment
+
+### Automated Deployment (Ubuntu 24.04)
+
+```bash
+sudo ./deploy.sh
+```
+
+The script handles:
+1. System updates and dependency installation (JDK 21, PostgreSQL, Nginx, Certbot)
+2. DNS verification for your domain
+3. JAR download and placement at `/opt/botmail/botmail.jar`
+4. PostgreSQL database and user creation
+5. System user (`botmail`) and directory structure
+6. DKIM key generation (RSA 2048-bit)
+7. Application properties generation
+8. SSL certificate (Let's Encrypt with self-signed fallback)
+9. Nginx reverse proxy configuration
+10. Systemd service setup and startup
+
+### Manual Deployment
+
+```bash
+# 1. Create directories
+mkdir -p /opt/botmail/logs
+mkdir -p /var/lib/botmail/data/mail
+mkdir -p /var/lib/botmail/dkim
+mkdir -p /var/lib/botmail/ssl
+
+# 2. Place files
+cp build/libs/botmail-2.8.0.jar /opt/botmail/botmail.jar
+cp application.properties /opt/botmail/
+
+# 3. Generate DKIM keys
+openssl genrsa -out /var/lib/botmail/dkim/private.pem 2048
+openssl rsa -in /var/lib/botmail/dkim/private.pem -pubout -out /var/lib/botmail/dkim/public.pem
+
+# 4. Run
+java --enable-preview --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED \
+     -Djava.library.path=/opt/botmail/native/linux-x86_64 \
+     -jar /opt/botmail/botmail.jar \
+     --spring.config.location=file:/opt/botmail/application.properties
+```
+
+### JVM Arguments
+
+```
+--enable-preview                          # Java 22 preview features
+--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED        # FFM API access
+-Djava.library.path=<native-libs-dir>     # Native library search path
+-Xms512m -Xmx1024m                       # Heap sizing (adjust as needed)
+```
+
+### Required Ports
+
+| Port | Protocol | Service |
+|------|----------|---------|
+| 25 | TCP | SMTP (inbound/outbound) |
+| 8080 | TCP | HTTP API (behind Nginx) |
+| 8888 | TCP | HTCPCP server |
+| 25565 | TCP | Minecraft server |
+| Configurable | TCP | Honeypot traps |
+
+### DNS Records
+
+```
+MX    @               → 10 mail.yourdomain.com.
+A     mail            → <server-ip>
+TXT   @               → v=spf1 mx ~all
+TXT   _dmarc          → v=DMARC1; p=none;
+TXT   mail._domainkey → v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=<public-key-base64>
+```
+
+### Systemd Service
+
+```ini
+[Unit]
+Description=LmyzMail Application
+After=network.target postgresql.service redis.service
+
+[Service]
+User=botmail
+Group=botmail
+WorkingDirectory=/opt/botmail
+CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE CAP_BPF CAP_NET_ADMIN
+AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE CAP_BPF CAP_NET_ADMIN
